BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INDICATORS: The Primordial Thread: Art\, Nature\, and the Human Bl
 ueprint
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T160000
UID:blogto-234805@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/08/original_image6c43917a-ac41-473a-83c9-5edc7d1486
 d9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:An Exclusive Davos Preview with Dr. Kerry Bowman\nHow is it th
 at indigenous communities\, separated by vast oceans and thousands of year
 s\, mirrored each other’s creative souls on the walls of silent caves?\n
 Before he takes the global stage at this year’s World Biodiversity Forum
  in Davos\, renowned bioethicist Dr. Kerry Bowman joins us for an intimate
  afternoon at Indicators. We will journey from the earliest marks of human
  consciousness to the present day\, exploring the profound\, universal con
 nection between our species and the natural world.\nThis isn’t just a hi
 story lesson\; it’s an exploration of the biological and spiritual "Indi
 cators" that define what it means to be human.\nWhat to Expect:\nA Global 
 Preview: Be among the first to engage with the insights Dr. Bowman is prep
 aring for the world stage.\nThe Universal Canvas: Discover the uncanny sim
 ilarities in indigenous cave art across the globe and what they reveal abo
 ut our shared psyche.\nIntimate Dialogue: A high-level talk in a curated s
 etting on the 22nd floor\, designed for creators\, thinkers\, and the natu
 re-curious.\nDETAILS:\nWhen: Saturday\, May 9\, 2026 | 2:00 PM\nWhere: 180
  Dundas St. West\, 22nd Floor\nAdmission: Complimentary (Light refreshment
 s will be served)\nNote: Seating is strictly limited to maintain an intima
 te atmosphere.\nTHIS EVENT WILL BE FILMED\nIndicators is presented in part
 nership with Crown Property Management and TENSANO.\nPhoto Source: The For
 est Health Alliance
LOCATION:180 Dundas St. W. 22nd Floor
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/indicators-the-primordial-thread-art-nat
 ure-and-the-human-blueprint-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
