BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chefs Table Junction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T203000
UID:blogto-233545@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:Heat Is On at Chef’s Table Junction 2026 — A Night of Culi
 nary Showdowns\, Cocktails & Community\nJunction\, Toronto — Monday\, Ma
 y 11\, 2026 - 6:30 PM. — Get ready for an electrifying evening of food\,
  flair\, and fierce (but friendly) competition as the Second Annual Chef
 ’s Table Junction returns to Rosario’s for one unforgettable night.\nS
 ix of the Junction’s most talented local chefs will go head-to-head in a
  high-stakes culinary battle for the coveted Chef’s Table Junction 2026 
 Champion title. The twist? Each chef will be handed a mystery ingredient b
 ox\, given just five minutes to raid the pantry\, and then race against th
 e clock with only one hour to craft a gourmet masterpiece worthy of our ce
 lebrity judges.\nGuests can expect more than just incredible food — this
  immersive experience includes complimentary light bites\, handcrafted coc
 ktails\, and a front-row seat to the action as creativity unfolds in real 
 time.\nFor those seeking the ultimate insider experience\, only 24 exclusi
 ve VIP Chef’s Table seats are available. These premium spots offer an up
 -close view of the culinary magic as it happens — from the first chop to
  the final plating.\nAdding to the excitement\, the ever-popular Silent Au
 ction returns with an array of must-have prizes. This year’s standout fe
 ature? A chance to bid on and taste the chefs’ actual competition dishes
  — putting you in the judge’s seat.  All proceeds go to the St. Joseph
  Hospital Foundation and the Junction Residents Association.\nThis lively 
 community fundraiser celebrates the vibrant local food scene while bringin
 g people together for a night of unforgettable entertainment.\nMark your c
 alendar\, bring your appetite\, and secure your spot — VIP seating is ex
 tremely limited and expected to sell out quickly.\nEvent Details:\n📍 Ro
 sario’s\, The Junction - 3030 Dundas Street West\n📅 Monday\, May 11\,
  2026\n🎟️ General Admission + Limited VIP Chef’s Table Experience A
 vailable\nCome hungry. Leave inspired.\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/chefs-
 table-junction-2026-at-rosarios-tickets-1984471461562?utm-campaign=social&
 utm-content=attendeeshare&utm-medium=discovery&utm-term=listing&utm-source
 =cp&aff=ebdsshcopyurl
LOCATION:Rosarios - 3030 Dundas Street West\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/chefs-table-junction-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crafting Grief: Mother's Day Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T200000
UID:blogto-233757@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imagec187ff55-41a2-4040-b773-9a0eb22f62
 74.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For some of us Mother's Day is a day of remembrance rather tha
 n celebration.\nJoin Adrianna\, a Death Doula and Grief Educator\, for a c
 ozy grief release through art.\nMay 11th\n7PM-8PM\nThe Plant Mystic\, 257 
 Danforth Ave\nRegister your spot: https://calendly.com/ladydeathdoula/craf
 ting-grief-mother-s-day-edition\n$33.33\nLet's lean into tradition and cra
 ft a Mother's Day card to help us metabolize our grief. Tea will be served
  so we can share a conversation about moms\, mothers\, mamas and the peopl
 e who are no longer with us that were a mother figure to us.\nOpen to thos
 e who are grieving the loss of their mother figure: estrangement\, death\,
  location disparity/separation.\nWhat to expect:\n-Sit down for tea\, sip 
 and share about your Mom\n-Make a mother's day card with craft supplies to
  take home for your ancestors altar\, as a keepsake\, or part of a memoria
 l\n-Light a candle in small ritual of remembrance for the mothers who are 
 no longer with us\nHosted by: Adrianna Prosser\, aka Lady Death Doula\, De
 ath Doula and Grief Educator\nYou might have seen Adrianna on CTV’s Th
 e Social as a special guest talking about the Death Positive Movement\, 
 or heard her on CBC Radio One across the country talking about grief and
  bereavement\, or in Canadian Business Magazine as a death industry disr
 uptor\, or liked one of her TikTok videos sharing her journey as a Death
  Doula. Adrianna’s brother Andrew died by suicide in 2010 and his death 
 catapulted her life into death work and mental health advocacy: she became
  a suicide awareness trainer and interventionist. Holding liminal space an
 d being comfortable in the discomfort has led Adrianna to become a hospic
 e volunteer and grief counselor. She is currently in a fast-tracked Bachel
 or’s of Social Work to become a grief therapist to complement all the t
 raining she has done as a death worker. Her practice is anti-oppressive\, 
 radically feminist\, and magically authentic to ensure she centers her com
 panions where they are at on their care journey. Join the death curious c
 onversation with her: @LadyDeathDoula on TikTok\, Instagram\, SubStack
LOCATION:The Plant Mystic
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/crafting-grief-mothers-day-edition-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eurovision Song Contest Trivia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T220000
UID:blogto-233573@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image4124e98b-1817-4ddc-bedc-a9303dc91a
 fb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Eurovision season is here! From iconic winners to unforgettabl
 e performances (and a few chaotic moments)\, this night is for the fans wh
 o know it all.\nExplore the songs\, stars\, and stories that shaped Eurovi
 sion\, from historic firsts to genre-defying winners and internet-famous p
 erformances.\nAssemble your team\, trust your instincts\, and may your ans
 wers earn the full douze points.\nKeeping the party going? Click the link 
 below to join us for one (or all) of our FREE Eurovision Watch Parties thi
 s week starting at 3PM on all three days!\nTRIVIA DETAILS\n🕕 Doors open
  at 6:00 PM. Arrive early\, grab a themed drink\, and get settled in.\n❓
  First question at 7:00 PM sharp. Don’t be late.\n🧠 Three rounds of t
 rivia\, about 15 questions each.\n🏆 The top three teams win a Pilot gif
 t card valued between $50 and $100.
LOCATION:The Pilot
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/eurovision-song-contest-trivia-toronto/
