BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Five Day Cake Baking & Decorating Masterclass
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T150000
UID:blogto-231764@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/04/original_image3a8de528-2ce2-4d9b-8a8c-82d662a988
 21.jpg
DESCRIPTION:If you've always dreamed of being a cake decorator\, this 5-da
 y masterclass is the perfect introduction to Cakes!\nThis class is perfect
  for absolute beginners! This is a 5 day course running for 5 hours each d
 ay.\nOUTLINE\nDAY 1: FOUNDATIONS OF CAKE BAKING AND BUTTERCREAM MAKING\nDA
 Y 2: MAKING A RAINBOW STRIPED CAKE\nDAY 3: FLORAL BUTTERCREAM PIPING TECHN
 IQUES\nDay 4: INTRODUCTION TO GUMPASTE AND FONDANT\nDay 5: STACKING & DECO
 RATING A TWO TIERED CAKE\nDAY 1: FOUNDATIONS OF CAKE BAKING AND BUTTERCREA
 M MAKING\nMix\, colour and bake a vanilla cake\nMake swiss meringue butter
 cream in groups\nLearn how to colour buttercream\nLearn how to use a pipin
 g bag and practicing piping design techniques\nDAY 2: MAKING A RAINBOW STR
 IPED CAKE\nLearn how to cut and layer your colourful cake\nLearn how to us
 e essential cake tools to achieve smooth straight sides on your cake\nLear
 n how create rainbow coloured stripes on the sides of your cake\nDAY 3: FL
 ORAL BUTTERCREAM PIPING TECHNIQUES\nHow to use piping bags and tips to dec
 orate cupcakes with buttercream\nHow to pipe a rose\, 5 petal flower and m
 um\nHow to pipe leaves and foliage to complete your cupcakes\nDay 4: INTRO
 DUCTION TO GUMPASTE AND FONDANT\nWhere to buy and how to store fondant and
  gumpaste\nHow to colour and mix fondant and gumpaste\nHow to use essentia
 l cake tools to achieve smooth straight sides on your cake\nHow to cover y
 our cake in fondant and which tools to use\nHow to use fondant cutouts to 
 decorate and finish your cake\nHow to add proper supports to your gumpaste
  teddy bear before placing on your finished cake\nDay 5: STACKING & DECORA
 TING A TWO TIERED CAKE\nHow to use piping bags and colours to decorate you
 r cake\nHow to use essential cake tools to achieve smooth straight sides o
 n you cake\nHow to properly add supports and stack a two tiered cake\nYou 
 will go home with:\nA one tier 6’’ round tall rainbow cake that you wi
 ll have decorated yourself on Day 2\nbuttercream flower cupcakes from Day 
 3\nA  fondant cake with gumpaste topper that you will have created on Day 
 4\nA two tiered buttercream cake flower cake on Day 5\nChocolate cake reci
 pe\, vanilla cake recipe\, Swiss meringue and American buttercream recipe\
 , emailed to you at the time of your booking\n‘How to use piping tips’
  recipe emailed to you at the time of your booking\nPictures are for displ
 ay purposes only. Your teacher will talk you through design elements in an
 y picture shown\, but for efficient running of this class\, you will be gu
 ided by her in terms of design.\nAll ingredients and equipment\, including
  transport boxes\, for your cake course are provided\, you do not need to 
 bring anything with you. The teacher will ensure that you work at a pace s
 uitable for you.\nIf you would like\, you can bring a large bag to carry y
 our cake(s) home. We provide sturdy cardboard boxes\, but you may find it 
 easier to carry your cake(s) in a reusable tote bag especially if taking p
 ublic transit to class.\n$899 + HST
LOCATION:Le Dolci Culinary School
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/five-day-cake-baking-decorating-mastercl
 ass-toronto-4/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lulaworld 2026: Marta Elena Album Release Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T220000
UID:blogto-234416@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_imageb7be6536-61e1-4a02-bade-d2bf78d45b
 5b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Powerhouse Cuban vocalist Marta Elena opens Lula's 2026 festiv
 al performing music from her sophomore album release Por Amor.\nSHOW DETAI
 LS\nPresave 'Mi Cafe Con Leche'\, the first track from the new album!\n7:0
 0 PM - Doors open for dinner and drinks. Reserve a table at lula.ca .\n8:0
 0 PM - Concert Begins\n$15 EARLY BIRD\n$20 ADVANCE\, $30 AT THE DOOR (DOES
  NOT GUARANTEE SEATING)\n$79 DINNER PACKAGE TICKETS INCLUDE 3-COURSE DINNE
 R\, SHOW & 18% GRATUITY\nEnjoy Lula's tropical-inspired dinner and drinks 
 menu before the show. Dinner reservations available at lula.ca/reservation
 s\nLulaworld Festival (May 11 to 17)\nJoin us at Lula Lounge to celebrate 
 the 20th annual Lulaworld festival\, marking two decades of local and inte
 rnational jazz\, Latin\, Brazilian\, soul and folk from around the globe a
 nd around the corner.\nOn this opening night of the festival\, we are high
 lighting the contributions of the Ontario Arts Council\, Ontario Creates a
 nd the Government of Ontario\, whose support makes it possible for us to p
 resent concerts\, workshops\, festivals and educational programs throughou
 t the year.\nMarta Elena\nWith special guest Hilario Duran!\nMarta Elena i
 s a Juno Award–winning Cuban singer\, composer\, and bandleader based in
  Toronto. Since relocating to Canada in 2011\, she has become a prominent 
 voice in the country’s Latin and jazz music scenes\, collaborating with 
 leading Canadian artists and performing at major venues and festivals nati
 onwide. As a Cuban vocalist\, composer\, and ensemble leader\, she embodie
 s the richness of the Cuban mulata tradition\, seamlessly blending genres 
 such as danzón\, rumba\, cha-cha-cha\, Cuban salsa\, and bolero.\nMarta E
 lena leads both a 13-piece orchestra and a sextet\, touring extensively ac
 ross Canada. She is a regular guest vocalist with Latin Grammy Award–win
 ning pianist Hilario Durán and his Latin Jazz Big Band\, and a lead vocal
 ist with the acclaimed all-female ensemble Maqueque\, directed by Jane Bun
 nett. Known for her powerful voice and commanding stage presence\, Marta E
 lena bridges Afro-Cuban tradition and contemporary Canadian music.\nAlbum:
  Por Amor\nMarta Elena returns with Por Amor\, a bold new album blending h
 er signature Cuban roots with boleros\, funk\, and regional Latin influenc
 es.\nRooted deeply in salsa\, Marta Elena honours the tradition that shape
 d her sound while boldly expanding its boundaries. On this album (Por Amor
 )\, she remains faithful to her salsa roots while embracing new musical co
 nversations\, weaving in bolero\, funk\, and regional influences that refl
 ect the evolving pulse of Latin American music worldwide.\nThis openness t
 o experimentation does not dilute her identity—it strengthens it\, posit
 ioning Marta Elena as an artist who bridges generations\, tradition and in
 novation\, and local histories with global sounds that are currently defin
 ing the Latin music scene on an international scale.\nPor Amor\, Marta Ele
 na’s new album\, was recorded at RHC Music Recording Studios in Toronto\
 , Canada\, with an exceptional group of Canadian musicians and renowned Cu
 ban- Canadian musicians based in the GTA. This album celebrates collaborat
 ion\, culture\, and love for music. Por Amor is dedicated to everyone who 
 has supported my musical journey.\nFollow Marta Elena on Instagram and Fac
 ebook.\nPresave or Listen to the track Mi Cafe Con Leche
LOCATION:Lula Lounge
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/lulaworld-2026-marta-elena-album-release
 -concert-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
