BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blood on the Clocktower at Twilight Cafe Downtown - Yonge & Bloor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T210000
UID:blogto-234199@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/26/original_imagea0e0e003-e896-4d26-ac16-d9d76a0b91
 01.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a seasoned gamer or new to the world of social 
 deception games\, this event offers something for everyone. Come solo or w
 ith friends and immerse yourself in a game of Blood on the Clocktower. Our
  events are a great way to connect with members of local communities and a
 re perfect for folks arriving in Toronto looking to make new connections.\
 nWhat is Blood on the Clocktower? - Blood on the Clocktower is an advanced
  version of the game Werewolf\, where crucially\, the dead still have an i
 mportant role to play in the game. The game is run by a Storyteller who ha
 s carefully crafted an experience and facilitates the game for up to 20 pl
 ayers. It is part deduction and part deception. Set in the town of Ravensw
 ood Bluff\, players in the game assume different roles\, each with unique 
 abilities to hunt down evil or manipulate the townsfolk.\nThanks to the ge
 nerosity of Twilight Cafe - Yonge & Bloor\, we will have plenty of space f
 or the night to engage in the social deduction of Blood on the Clocktower.
  Twilight Cafe has a menu with food and both alcoholic and nonalcoholic be
 verages that you can order from while we’re having fun deducing and dece
 iving. Tickets for this event are $20 or $13.50 for Changeling Special Eve
 nts Members.\nIf you have not played before or are newer to the game\, the
 re will be a quick tutorial at the top of the event to learn how to play a
 nd ask any questions from the Storyteller.\nWe will be playing Trouble Bre
 wing at this event.\nAge recommendation\, 16 years +\nTo learn more\, find
  Changeling Gaming Events Toronto on Eventbrite or click the website link 
 to see this event (see right side on desktop/above on mobile).
LOCATION:Twilight Cafe - Yonge & Bloor
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/blood-on-the-clocktower-at-twilight-cafe
 -downtown-yonge-bloor-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Game Designer Night at Bickford Brewing in Downtown Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T220000
UID:blogto-234198@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/26/original_image371bbcb9-f0ff-47e1-9a4f-97d9f17213
 77.jpg
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a fun night of testing out intere
 sting new board games in the process of being designed. Bring your own des
 ign and we'll do our best to ensure everyone gets their turn on the table!
 \nWhether you're a seasoned gamer or new to the world of board games\, eve
 ryone has useful feedback to provide. Test out new games\, challenge your 
 friends\, and make new connections with fellow board game lovers along the
  way. Come as a group or solo and we can help pair you with a community ta
 ble. Our events are a great way to connect with members of local communiti
 es and are perfect for folks arriving in Toronto looking to meet new peopl
 e.\nThanks to the generosity of Bickford Brewing\, we will be enjoying the
  use of their space for our night of learning and playtesting new\, in-pro
 cess board games. Bickford Brewing has a selection of empanadas and pizza 
 to eat along with both alcoholic and nonalcoholic beverages to enjoy while
  we’re having fun playing games. This event is Pay-What-You-Can (minimum
  $5) or free for Changeling Members\, with more details available at the l
 ink to the Changeling Gaming Events Eventbrite (see website link).\nTo lea
 rn more\, find Changeling Gaming Events Toronto on Eventbrite or click the
  website link to see this event (see right side on desktop/above on mobile
 ).
LOCATION:Bickford Brewing
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/board-game-designer-night-at-bickford-br
 ewing-in-downtown-toronto-toronto/
