BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Abendmusik: from Buxtehude to Bach
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T210000
UID:blogto-233749@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/16/original_image0e3e5063-4386-4ee8-b485-b80452e105
 16.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Experience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach\nIn 1705\,
  the 20-year-old Johann Sebastian Bach journeyed 400 kilometres on foot fr
 om Arnstadt to Lübeck to meet and learn from the great composer Dietrich 
 Buxtehude\, then aged 70. During Bach’s three-month stay he would have e
 xperienced Buxtehude’s legendary Abendmusiken\, or “Evening Concer
 ts”\, with their mix of sacred vocal and instrumental music presented in
  St. Mary’s Church.\nOur own special Abendmusik invites you to exper
 ience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach\, and meet other musical tr
 avellers along the way: Johann Christoph Bach\, Graupner\, Doles\, Reincke
 n and Krebs.\nCome\, refresh your spirit and soul with our Abendmusik 
 offering\, featuring the Tafelmusik Chamber Choir and members of the Tafel
 musik Baroque Orchestra. Buy your tickets for Abendmusik: from Buxtehude t
 o Bach on May 15\, 2026 at tafelmusik.org
LOCATION:Jeanne Lamon Hall\, Trinity-St. Paul’s Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/abendmusik-from-buxtehude-to-bach-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Creative Wellbeing Gathering - Hiphop Soundbath & Networking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T210000
UID:blogto-234601@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_imageab1fe89c-58cd-4a46-a32a-4f5a2b67e3
 4c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A Fundraising Evening for Wellbeing\, Creativity & Community\n
 We are hosting a special Mindful Creative Gathering — an intimate fundra
 ising evening designed for Torontonians across wellbeing\, wellness\, and 
 creative communities.\nThis is a space where mindfulness\, hip-hop\, and c
 reative expression come together to explore a deeper question: How do we c
 are for ourselves — and for each other?\nAt the heart of this gathering 
 is our belief: Mental Wellbeing → Community Wellbeing.\nAn immersive eve
 ning featuring:\n• Guided hip-hop meditation & sound bath\n• Live musi
 c performance\n• Storytelling and cultural expression\n• Meaningful co
 nnection and community gathering\n• Book signing and mindfulness merch\n
 Featured Guest:\nBorn I (Ofosu Jones-Quartey) is a Ghanaian-American artis
 t\, author\, and mindfulness teacher working at the intersection of hip-ho
 p and Buddhism.\nBlending poetic lyricism with contemplative insight\, his
  work explores self-compassion\, presence\, and liberation. He is the auth
 or of Lyrical Dharma: Hip-Hop as Mindfulness and the creator of the Hip-Ho
 p Soundbath — a live experience weaving meditation\, music\, and sound h
 ealing.\nWe are inviting:\n• Toronto’s wellness and mindfulness commun
 ity\n• creatives\, artists\, and cultural practitioners\n• young profe
 ssionals seeking balance and meaning\n• community builders and social im
 pact leaders\nWhether you come from a meditation background\, a creative p
 ractice — or both — this is a space to meet at the intersection.\nRSVP
  (limited tickets): https://www.wisdomwayimpact.com/event-details/mindful-
 af-a-creative-wellbeing-gathering\nYour participation supports the growth 
 of our community work\, including mental wellbeing programs\, creative gat
 herings\, and accessible spaces for connection.\nHosted by Wisdomway Impac
 t\nDJ & Host: DJ Devo\nHip-hop meditation\, sound bath & performance: Born
  I\nVenue Partner: 520 Cafe Bar
LOCATION:520 Cafe Bar
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-creative-wellbeing-gathering-hiphop-so
 undbath-networking-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
