ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/01/original_imagef4860197-6080-42fa-bd74-16efb4e933
 35.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Loohoo Kawaii Market is taking over Queen St W this May and it
 's going to be SO cute\nIf your idea of a perfect weekend involves sticker
 s\, handmade goods\, fanart merch\, and being surrounded by the most adora
 ble indie makers in the city — Loohoo Kawaii Market is calling your name
  🌸\nRunning Saturday May 16 and Sunday May 17\, 2026 from 11 AM – 6 P
 M\, the Kawaii Market is back at Loohoo (1380 Queen St W) for two full day
 s of curated indie art\, kawaii culture\, and the kind of finds you won't 
 stop thinking about. Entry is free.\nThe vendor lineup for this little mar
 ket is stacked!\n@jeffery.kingsley brings pastel pink\, queer joy\, and fu
 zzy creature energy through stickers\, zines\, charms\, and original art. 
 Calling all furries!\n@hitoruki_shop is your one-stop for fanart goodies s
 panning JRPGs\, otome games\, and everything in between — think Love and
  Deepspace\, Persona\, Obey Me\, and Deltarune.\n@episodesofjoy makes the 
 most heartwarming stationery around\, featuring Loki the rescue Samoyed re
 imagined as a dango\, a cup noodle\, a mochi — all the Asian snacks.\n@j
 unijuni.studio offers hand-painted small-batch ceramics that are functiona
 l\, collectible\, and completely one of a kind. Your favourite anime in a 
 mug awaits you.\n@meomade.art brings Toronto-inspired prints alongside the
 ir cult-favourite handmade clay magnets and pins. Find all the aliens spri
 nkled through the art!\n@smallbitecrafts is doing crochet hair accessories
 \, plushies\, and — yes — pet hats for your fur pals!\n@snoozy.bun is 
 pastel rainbow Care Bear energy in pin and sticker form.\n@peachtree.studi
 o makes the cutest crochet and art\n@dreamdoodle brings doodle art inspire
 d by Toronto\, nature\, and culture.\n@mintyy_artz turns anime fanart into
  charms\, stickers\, and prints made with a lot of love and late nights.\n
 @littolichi features original characters Bunny the Bunny and Cosy the Bear
  across stationery\, glass tumblers\, suncatcher decals\, and more.\nWheth
 er you're a fanart collector\, a crochet girlie\, a stationery hoarder\, o
 r just someone who thinks cute things are a form of self care — there is
  genuinely something here for you.\n📍 Loohoo\, 1380 Queen St W\, Toront
 o\n📅 Saturday May 16 + Sunday May 17\, 2026\n🕚 11 AM – 6 PM\n🎟
 ️ Free entry
LOCATION:Loohoo
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/loohoo-kawaii-market-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
