BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Democracy Under Siege
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T173800
UID:blogto-233555@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image9658635c-95d9-488d-afa1-27026fe69e
 01.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Punctuated by the sharp and witty political commentary of Puli
 tzer-prize winning editorial cartoonist Ann Telnaes (Washington Post) from
  her bird’s eye view in the cat seat of the United States capital\, Wash
 ington D.C.\, top political analysts lay bare the complex history and chal
 lenges of the world’s most influential political system. Oscar-nominated
  Director Laura Nix trains her insightful lens on one of American democrac
 y’s most extreme and vital moments in its nearly 250 years of existence.
  The film connects present-day crises with their roots in American history
  via commentary with A-list political observers who explore executive over
 reach\, a crisis in judicial ethics\, and a media environment saturated wi
 th disinformation\, as the country grapples with fundamental challenges th
 at transcend individual presidencies. With innovative dark humor\, the fil
 m examines how the promise of American multiracial democracy faces a renew
 ed backlash\, culminating in fears of an actual authoritarian takeover.\nC
 an the nation preserve its democratic ideals amidst severe polarization an
 d a political party which has embraced extremism?\nJoin director Laura Nix
  and subject Ann Telnaes for a special post-screening discussion on Saturd
 ay\, May 30.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/democracy-under-siege-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Joan Beckow: Musical Theatre's Overlooked Gem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T143000
UID:blogto-234637@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_image3ecdcec8-623a-46b0-a705-acd9041b21
 8a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever heard of Canadian songwriter and composer Joan B
 eckow? Probably not. But we hope to change that with Back Lane Studios' ne
 xt Extraordinary Women event on Sunday\, May 17\, 12:30pm at the Revue Cin
 ema.\nBeckow was a musical theatre talent. Her work has been likened to th
 at of Stephen Sondheim and Leonard Bernstein. She was an early friend and 
 collaborator of Carol Burnett\, whose career Beckow helped launch by compo
 sing songs for her.\nJoin us at the Revue\, Sunday\, May 17 to hear Beckow
 's music performed live by four musicians\, watch a short documentary "Uns
 ung: The Joan Beckow Story\," and enjoy a Q&A with the directors Jessica S
 tuart and Wendy Bross Stuart\, who for years was Beckow's arranger and col
 laborator.\nJessica and Wendy launched the Joan Beckow Legacy Project\, fu
 nded by the Canada Council and others\, to make the documentary and record
  Beckow's music. They join singers Alex Samaras and Whitney Ross-Barris fo
 r our mini-concert at the Revue.\nBorn in 1933 in the United States\, Beck
 ow studied music at UCLA and moved to New York City with Burnett. But soon
  she would marry\, immigrate to Vancouver and focus her talents on raising
  her family\, while sharing her music with her community.\nShe continued c
 omposing and working with Canadian theatre groups. She also mounted a numb
 er of her own musicals in Vancouver. Meanwhile\, she trained as a music th
 erapist and taught at Capilano College.\nBeckow passed away in 2021.\nBuy 
 tickets in advance for a suggested donation of $20 in advance on Eventbrit
 e  or $25 at the door.
LOCATION:Revue Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/joan-beckow-musical-theatres-overlooked-
 gem-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
