BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:METAMOOD: An Afternoon of Readings and Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T153000
UID:blogto-234148@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/24/original_image324e0407-0198-4dc0-8c67-f9b4be775e
 dd.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Metatron Press x In the Mood Magazine are pleased to announce 
 METAMOOD in Toronto\, an afternoon celebrating our vibrant literary ecosys
 tem and the launch of Wavering Futures by Kawai Shen!\nTICKETS: https://ww
 w.eventbrite.ca/e/metamood-a-reading-tickets-1987649614503\nWe humbly invi
 te you to dream and conspire with us about the future of art and literatur
 e amid great uncertainty. You can expect a banging line-up of readings\, w
 ordy activities\, friendly faces\, a fundraiser for land defenders\, and r
 eal talk about what it means to build creative communities today. There wi
 ll be spice! 🌶️🍵\nFeaturing readings by:\n✽ Kawai Shen\n✽ Senn
 ah Yee\n✽ Trynne Delaney\n✽ Nirris Nagendrarajah\n✽ Lee Suksi\nReadi
 ngs will be followed by a collective discussion led by Ashley Obscura (fou
 nder\, Metatron Press)\, Gabrielle Marceau & Sennah Yee (founders\, In the
  Mood Magazine)\, and Kawai Shen (author\, Wavering Futures) about how to 
 keep dreaming through our collective nightmare\, sustain creative practice
 s\, survive our era of existential crises (together)\, and make connection
 s of support\, care\, and inspiration. We invite audience participation.\n
 Please bring your attention\, ideas\, goodwill\, and honesty. No recording
 s will be permitted ♡\nEach ticket includes entry into a fundraising raf
 fle. A % of the proceeds will be donated to Grassy Narrows First Nation’
 s land defence.\nAccessibility notes:\n- Accessible venue with ground-floo
 r accessible washroom\n- All washrooms are gender neutral\n- Masking is en
 couraged! 😷\n- Free N-95 (limited supply) and surgical masks at the doo
 r\n- Space is large and will run two HEPA air purifiers (Winix C 535) by s
 eating area\n- We will leave front doors open for air circulation (weather
  permitting)\n- Water will be provided\n- Comfortable sofa seating\n- Plea
 se contact us about ASL interpretation\nIf you have any other accessibilit
 y questions or requests\, please do not hesitate to contact us via Eventbr
 ite.\nMetatron Press: https://metatron.press/\nIn The Mood Magazine: https
 ://www.inthemoodmagazine.com/
LOCATION:It's Ok* Studios
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/metamood-an-afternoon-of-readings-and-di
 scussion-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mother Effers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T190000
UID:blogto-234429@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_image8fce073e-d0dd-4c6e-b6cd-49a25b8e76
 58.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Comedy for and by parents that will get you home before bedtim
 e!\nAnna Penner (@somequeerreads): Anna is Toronto-based comedian\, a pare
 nt of many\, and a former member of the Manitoba Ferret Owners Association
 . Their comedy blends sharp observations with a conversational style\, as 
 they find the laughs in sexuality\, gender\, parenting\, and day-to-day li
 fe.\nKristin Doucet (@kristindoucet): Armed with sharp wit\, zero shame an
 d no f&*%ks left to give\, Kristin draws on life as a daughter of aging pa
 rents\, a sometimes-good wife\, and a not-half-bad mom to two teenagers. K
 ristin mines the chaos of menopause\, marriage\, motherhood and the mundan
 e into hilarious storytelling with a self-depracting approach that would m
 ake Joan Rivers proud.\nTogether\, Anna and Kristin are two parents trying
  to make it in the world of comedy and parenting. Exhausted\, broke and qu
 estioning their life choices\, they tackle every stage\, from the Terrible
  Twos to the Turbulent Teen Years and everything in between. Featuring a l
 ineup of comedians who are parents themselves\, this show delivers brutall
 y honest\, laugh-until-you-cry stories from the parenting trenches.\nFeatu
 ring :\nMatt Bee @mattbeecomedy\nPrecious Chong @preciousshelbychong\nCaro
 lina DG @caro_deegee\nJessica Rosenberg @jessicagbr\nJamal Ryan Severin-Wa
 tson @the_gucci_champion\nHeadliner: The amazing Zabrina Douglas @zabrinad
 ouglas\nTickets are $25
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/mother-effers-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
