BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Python Hunt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T200000
UID:blogto-233629@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image730be97d-b457-4520-b484-69613cfe11
 da.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Special Jury Award Winner - 2025 SXSW Film Festival\nThe Pytho
 n Hunt is an “irresistible cocktail of vigilantism\, competition and nat
 ure conservation” (Stephen Saito\, The Moveable Fest). This entertaining
  film about Floridian life is also the first ever documentary to be made a
 bout competitive python hunting. Every year\, the Florida government calls
  upon the general public to compete in an invasive python removal contest 
 in the Everglades in an attempt to save the threatened ecosystem. The film
  follows the conquests of several of the contest’s more memorable compet
 itors.\nWhile focusing on the plight of these python hunters would make fo
 r a thrilling enough story\, The Python Hunt has more on its mind\, includ
 ing a critical viewpoint on the overall impact of the hunt. Not content to
  merely find amusement in the antics of some Florida-based eccentrics\, di
 rector Xander Robin and producer Lance Oppenheim (Ren Faire\, Spermworld\,
  Some Kind of Heaven) offer a humane look at the lives of several individu
 als who enroll in the Challenge for various reasons (to impress others? To
  gain a following on social media? To prove something about their masculin
 ity?)\, as well as one memorable character who is struggling to find a new
  lease on life after being blacklisted from participating.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-python-hunt-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Freestyle Glow-in-the-Dark Painting: Self-Guided Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260518T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260518T180000
UID:blogto-234072@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/22/original_image15829efd-9616-4f2e-873d-92dbbbeba6
 a5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Step into a glowing\, immersive art experience where creativit
 y will literally shine. Under UV lighting\, explore bold expression using 
 neon and glow-in-the-dark paints in a unique studio setting designed to in
 spire.\nWhat to Expect\nThis self-guided session blends art and atmosphere
  for a visually striking\, sensory-driven experience. Inside our glow stud
 io\, you’ll work with vibrant neon pigments that transform under blackli
 ght—creating artwork that is dynamic\, expressive\, and completely your 
 own.\nSelf-Guided Format\nEnjoy the freedom to create at your own pace. Wh
 ether you choose to freehand your design or trace a pre-selected image\, o
 ur team will be available for light guidance and support as needed. Go abs
 tract or paint a glowing scene\; all you need is an open mind to tap into 
 your creative side.\nAll Materials Included\nYour session includes access 
 to premium neon and glow-in-the-dark paints\, brushes\, and all necessary 
 art materials. Aprons are provided\, but we recommend wearing white or neo
 n tones to enhance the glow experience—and clothing you don’t mind get
 ting a little paint on.\nWho This Is For\nThis experience is ideal for adu
 lts and older kids\, date nights\, and creative outings with friends. Must
  be aged 10+ to participate.  Guests 16+ may attend independently\; younge
 r participants are welcome when accompanied by an adult. You’re welcome 
 to work individually or share a canvas. See the Family Paint sessions for 
 guests younger than 10.\nParticipants are asked to arrive anytime between 
 7-8 pm.\nSee more events at: https://www.artboxstudiogallery.com/calendar\
 nCall us at: 647-617-9550
LOCATION:Artbox Studio Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-freestyle-glow-in-the-dark-painting-se
 lf-guided-experience-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
