ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_imaged9a47160-d33d-4afb-82de-941f40cd6b
 67.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come on Boot\, it's roll call for The Rookie Trivia! From patr
 ol to high-stakes ops\, prove you know the drama at the Mid-Wilshire Divis
 ion.\nFrom John Nolan’s late start in the LAPD to high-stakes cases\, in
 tense training\, and evolving partnerships (i.e. #Chenford )\, this night 
 covers the biggest moments from The Rookie.\nExpect questions on key story
 lines\, character arcs\, unforgettable cases\, and the dynamics that keep 
 the precinct running.\nWhether you’re here for the action or the team\, 
 bring your crew and prove you’ve got what it takes to make the cut.\nTRI
 VIA DETAILS\n🕕 Doors open at 6:00 PM. Arrive early\, grab a themed drin
 k\, and get settled in.\n❓ First question at 7:00 PM sharp. Don’t be l
 ate.\n🧠 Three rounds of trivia\, about 15 questions each.\n🏆 The top
  three teams win a Hem’s gift card valued between $50 and $100.
LOCATION:Hemingway's
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-rookie-trivia-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Island Photo Walk and Dusk Skyline Adventure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T172000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T213000
UID:blogto-234729@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/06/original_image3bd23507-1d9a-4bb6-b2ff-0b7b6d56bd
 d7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In this 3+ hour event\, we will photograph various features of
  the Toronto island (fauna\, attractions\, and still life subjects) follow
 ed by an exercise in long exposure photography of the famous Toronto city 
 skyline through the twilight period.\nThis photography adventure is for an
 yone who owns an interchangeable lens DSLR or mirrorless camera and a full
  size tripod. You will learn how to adjust manual settings to accommodate 
 for the changing light and capture a handful of majestic print worthy phot
 ographs of the skyline as the sun sets.\nNO MANUAL MODE EXPERIENCE NEEDED!
  You will receive detailed guidance throughout the evening to learn how to
  control your settings on your camera.\nYou will need:\n- Interchangeable 
 lens DSLR or mirrorless camera\n- Lens with focal lengths ranging from 24-
 70 mm\, approx. Wide lenses recommended for the skyline shots\, higher foc
 al length for 'walkabout' photography on the island\n- Full size tripod\n-
  Clothing suitable for the evening time on the island\, which can be chill
 y\n- Optional mosquito spray (may not be needed\, but just in case)\n- Wat
 er bottle\, energy bar or similar snack\nAll details including when and wh
 ere to meet on the island will be provided by email to all registered atte
 ndees. Departure from the Jack Layton ferry terminal is approximately 5:20
 pm\, meeting on the island after the ferry crosses (15-20 mins)\nRain date
  will be May 20 if rain is forecast for the event date of May 19 in the ev
 ening. Paid attendees will be informed earlier in the day if the trip is p
 ostponed due to weather.\nCost to attend: $129 per attendee\, payable on w
 ww.cameraschool.ca\nFull event details are here: https://cameraschool.ca/t
 oronto-island-photo-walk\nPlease note\, this event involves a significant 
 amount of walking as we move to different locations prior to the main even
 t of the Toronto skyline. This event is not recommended for those with mob
 ility issues.
LOCATION:Centre Island Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-island-photo-walk-and-dusk-skyli
 ne-adventure-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
