DESCRIPTION:Nature-Inspired Afternoons\nIn this after school program\, chi
 ldren explore the vibrant world of birds and plants through art\, science\
 , exhibit visits\, and outdoor play. Inspired by David Salazar's: Bird Bot
 anicals exhibit\, each week blends creativity with nature discovery.\nWeek
 ly Themes:\nMay 20: Feathered Friends - Bird mask-making\, feather science
 \, bird call games.\nMay 27: Botanical Prints - Leaf printing\, nature wal
 k\, plant identification.\nJune 3: Nest Builders - Build nests with natura
 l materials\, egg experiments.\nJune 10: Pollinator Party - Butterfly craf
 ts\, pollination relay\, garden scavenger hunt.\nJune 17: Birds & Botanica
 ls Collage - Mixed media art\, storytelling with bird characters.\nJune 24
 : Nature Journals - Drawing exhibit favourites\, nature walk sketches.\nTi
 ckets: https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/cityofpickering/activity/s
 earch?activity_select_param=2&activity_keyword=after-school&viewMode=list
