 04.jpg
DESCRIPTION:1 in 6 people globally are now affected by loneliness\, with s
 ignificant impacts on their health and well-being. Whereas social connecti
 on can protect health across the lifespan – reducing inflammation\, impr
 oving mental health and lowering the risk of serious health problems. Wher
 e we live can also play a big role in helping us feel more connected. Join
  us online on May 20 to learn more about loneliness\, its impact on health
 \, and to understand how communities\, especially naturally occurring reti
 rement communities (NORCs)\, can support stronger relationships and health
 ier aging.\n\nAbout the Series:\nBridging Minds: Health & Science Conversa
 tions is a partnership between the Toronto Public Library and Women’s Co
 llege Hospital. Through monthly discussions led by experts from across cli
 nical areas and scientific disciplines\, this series provides attendees wi
 th the opportunity to engage directly with our topics and speakers and emp
 owers communities to navigate health and science topics with confidence\, 
 inspiring a future of informed decision-making.\nReserve Your Spot Today!\
 nThis virtual event is free to join\, but registration is required. Once r
 egistered\, you’ll receive an email with details on how to join the sess
 ion.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/bridging-minds-health-science-conversati
 ons-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
