BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Car Mechanics Workshop in North York
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T130000
UID:blogto-234366@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_imageac4a1b86-f453-4c10-8081-b00b79a931
 7d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Learn basic car mechanics in this hands-on beginner workshop\,
  no experience needed.\nThis 3-hour class gives you the practical skills a
 nd confidence to take care of your own vehicle. Whether you're a new car o
 wner\, tired of relying on someone else\, or just done feeling lost at the
  shop\, this is the course for you. Total beginners welcome\, ages 16+\, i
 n a judgment-free\, supportive space.\nWhat you'll learn:\n✅ Pop the hoo
 d\, check fluids\, replace filters\, and jumpstart an engine\n✅ Change a
  tire\, check tread depth and air pressure\, inflate a tire\, and examine 
 your brakes\n✅ Know-how to keep you safe during roadside emergencies and
  avoid costly repairs\n✅ A simple maintenance plan — you'll work with 
 a mechanic to build a routine that fits your specific vehicle\nWhy people 
 sign up:\nFlat tires\, low oil\, a dead battery - emergencies happen. For 
 a lot of people\, even a routine mechanic visit can feel intimidating. Man
 y of our attendees come in tired of overpaying for simple repairs\, or of 
 having to call someone every time a dashboard light comes on. In three hou
 rs\, you'll have the skills to handle the basics yourself and the confiden
 ce to ask the right questions when you do go to a shop.\nMeet Your Instruc
 tor:\nOur instructor is a licensed mechanic with 20+ years of experience. 
 He has taught auto mechanics to hundreds of students at all levels
LOCATION:Spaces United
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/beginner-car-mechanics-workshop-in-north
 -york-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brain Power Lab on How to be Punny Using Puns and Jokes to Build V
 ocabulary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T144500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T154500
UID:blogto-234187@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/26/original_image15ebe092-3f45-4f5d-a125-889c1abcc5
 c1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The "How to be Punny: Using Puns and Jokes to Build Vocabulary
 " learning lab is a unique and engaging opportunity for students in Grades
  2-4 to expand their vocabulary in a fun and interactive way. This exclusi
 ve lab\, led by a Brain Power vocabulary expert\, builds on what students 
 are learning in class and focuses on developing their language skills thro
 ugh humor and wordplay.\nThe lab begins with a warm welcome and an introdu
 ction\, where students are greeted enthusiastically and introduced to the 
 concept of learning new words through puns and jokes. The session is desig
 ned to be both educational and entertaining\, with activities that are car
 efully scaffolded by age to ensure appropriate challenges for all particip
 ants.\nThe lesson portion introduces students to the concept of puns and j
 okes:\n-Puns: Defined as jokes that use the different possible meanings of
  a word or words that sound alike but have different meanings. The lab use
 s examples and funny explanations to help students understand and enjoy th
 e wordplay.\n-Jokes: Defined as something said or done to make people laug
 h. Students explore various types of jokes\, including homophone and homog
 raph puns\, and riddles\, with the vocabulary expert providing explanation
 s and encouraging discussion.\nInteractive activities are tailored to the 
 age group and designed to engage students in creating and understanding pu
 ns and jokes. This approach not only helps students enhance their vocabula
 ry but also fosters creativity and confidence in using language. The lab c
 oncludes with a recap and the awarding of Pun Master certificates\, recogn
 izing each student's participation and achievements.\nThis lab is perfect 
 for students looking to strengthen their vocabulary skills in a supportive
  and fun environment\, guided by an expert in the field.
LOCATION:De La Salle College
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/brain-power-lab-on-how-to-be-punny-using
 -puns-and-jokes-to-build-vocabulary-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
