 gto.com/events/2026/05/04/original_image7f36ba91-bcfd-487c-98f0-8876d9998a
 58.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Heading outdoors - The Cookstown Antique and Vintage show\nThe
  Cookstown Antique and Vintage show\, coming up May 23\, takes place outdo
 ors on a ten acre field.  More than eighty dealers\, 160-odd tables\, on t
 he grass at the Steam Show Grounds in Cookstown.\nThere's a special vibe a
 round an outdoor antique show.  In spacious surroundings\, on grassy field
 s\, dealers bring larger loads - lots more to see.  The food trucks are cr
 anking out their specialties.  You can smell the onions frying!  No questi
 on - strolling around a lovely outdoor venue is a great way to shop for an
 tiques and vintage.\nTrucks packed to the doors are coming from all parts 
 of Ontario - including a dozen from Simcoe County - plus half a dozen from
  Quebec.  This makes for real diversity - shoppers can find hundreds of ca
 tegories of furniture and collectibles.\nThe Steam Show grounds are at 463
 5 Victoria St. W. in Cookstown.  The show runs Saturday\, May 23 from 8am 
 until 4pm.  Admission is $12\, kids under 13 are free and on-site parking 
 is also free.
LOCATION:The Steam Show Grounds\, 4635 Victoria St W.\, Cookstown
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/cookstown-outddor-antique-and-vintage-sh
 ow-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
