BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sashbear Walk for Mental Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T130000
UID:blogto-233226@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/06/original_imagea1734d95-3669-4a8c-b144-522bef3333
 e7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the 14th annual Sashbear Walk on May 24 at Sir Casi
 mir Gzowski Park from 9 am to 1 pm. The Sashbear Walk has been an annual e
 vent since 2013\, bringing together families\, friends\, those with lived 
 experience\, mental health providers and supporters throughout the communi
 ty to create a sea of orange in support of those with emotion dysregulatio
 n.\nThis annual walk is the largest event of its kind in Canada for emotio
 n dysregulation and borderline personality disorder. People come together 
 to raise awareness\, reduce stigma\, and make waves for mental health—a 
 journey to provide hope of a life worth living\, for all.
LOCATION:Sir Casimir Gzowski Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sashbear-walk-for-mental-health-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Somatic Skills Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T153000
UID:blogto-234249@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_image489e4210-c73f-4e66-b6a3-8172793124
 91.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Many of us are feeling dysregulated (overwhelmed\, anxious\, d
 isconnected or numb)\,at least some of the time. This is understandable an
 d is a natural response to the internal and external stress\, change\, dis
 ruption or uncertainty.\nThe path of return to regulation is in the body\,
  the home of our highly sensitive nervous system. Join us in this experien
 tial immersion as we work mindfully with somatic practices designed to sup
 port nervous system regulation and healing.\nIn this workshop you will be 
 compassionately accompanied through movement\, breath\, voice/sound and re
 flective journaling to reconnect with yourself and to gain tools to cultiv
 ate a greater sense of calm\, groundedness and flow.
LOCATION:Breathe Yoga Studio
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/somatic-skills-workshop-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
