 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image29c3824e-1c4d-4612-a73c-01db14c469
 bc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Remember the chaos\, cases\, and high-stakes shifts at The Pit
 t Trivia! Test your knowledge of the ER\, the team\, and every intense mom
 ent.\nWelcome to The Pitt.\nFrom chaotic ER shifts and life-or-death decis
 ions to the team dynamics that keep it all together\, this trivia night di
 ves into the intensity of The Pitt.\nExpect questions on major cases\, cha
 racter arcs\, hospital politics\, and the moments that pushed everyone to 
 their limits.\nAssemble your team\, think fast\, and trust your instincts 
 because in this room\, every answer counts.\nTRIVIA DETAILS\n🕕 Doors op
 en at 6:00 PM. Arrive early\, grab a themed drink\, and get settled in.\n
 ❓ First question at 7:00 PM sharp. Don’t be late.\n🧠 Three rounds o
 f trivia\, about 15 questions each.\n🏆 The top three teams win a Hem’
 s gift card valued between $50 and $100.
LOCATION:Hemingway's
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-pitt-trivia-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ultimate Dim Sum Experience at Wok Theory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T210000
UID:blogto-234319@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_imageef56874e-c6df-4110-ada3-e7a112ccb9
 6b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This event takes place at Wok Theory\, 530 Dundas St W\, Toron
 to. [MAP]\nJoin restaurateur Edwin Lam and The Depanneur's Len Senater for
  a remarkable 12+ course gastronomic foray into the world of dim sum. This
  event will also feature an exclusive dumpling making demonstration by Wok
  Theory Executive Dim Sum Chef Trinh Tieu.\nDim sum is a traditional Chine
 se culinary practice centred on small\, shareable dishes typically enjoyed
  with tea. Its roots trace back to southern China\, especially the Cantone
 se-speaking regions like Guangdong Province and the city of Guangzhou. The
  term dim sum literally means “touch the heart\,” reflecting the idea 
 of light bites meant to satisfy rather than overwhelm.\nHistorically\, dim
  sum is closely tied to the culture of Yum Cha\, which translates to “dr
 ink tea.” This tradition began along ancient trade routes\, where travel
 lers and merchants would stop at teahouses to rest. Initially\, tea was be
 lieved to aid digestion\, and food was not always served alongside it. Ove
 r time\, small snacks were introduced\, eventually evolving into the wide 
 array of dishes now associated with dim sum. By the time of the Qing Dynas
 ty (1644–1912)\, teahouses in southern China had become vibrant social h
 ubs\, and dim sum had grown into a refined culinary art.\nA defining featu
 re of dim sum is its variety. Dishes range from steamed dumplings like Har
  Gow and Siu Mai to buns such as Char Siu Bao\, as well as rice rolls\, sp
 ring rolls\, and desserts. Traditionally\, these items are served in small
  bamboo steamers or on small plates\, allowing diners to sample multiple f
 lavours and textures in a single meal.\nTea plays an essential role in the
  tradition. Popular choices include Jasmine tea\, Pu-erh tea\, and Oolong 
 tea. Etiquette is important: pouring tea for others before oneself is cust
 omary\, and a gentle tapping of fingers on the table is a traditional way 
 to express thanks.\nToday\, dim sum has spread far beyond China\, becoming
  a global phenomenon in cities with large Chinese communities\, from Hong 
 Kong to Toronto and San Francisco. While modern variations may include fus
 ion elements or made-to-order service instead of carts\, the essence of di
 m sum—variety\, sharing\, and connection—remains unchanged.\n-----\n
 蝦餃 Har Gow - Supreme Shrimp Dumplings\n燒賣 Siu Mai - Pork & Shrimp 
 Dumplings with Fish Roe\n什菌南瓜餃 Mo Gu Nam Gwa Gow - Mushrooms & P
 umpkin Dumplings\nTea: 普洱茶 Po Lei - aka Pu-erh\, a black tea common 
 in dim sum restaurants\n叉燒包 Char Siu Bao - Steamed BBQ Pork Bun\n鳳
 爪 Fung Jow - Chicken Feet with House Special Sauce\n珍珠雞 Gai Lo Mai
  Fan - Sticky Rice with Chicken and Egg Yolk in Lotus Leaf\nTea: 香片 He
 ung Pin - fragrant jasmine green tea\n芋角 Heung So Wu Gok Gai - Crispy 
 Taro Puffs with Chicken\n蘿蔔糕 Lap Cheung Jin Lo Bak Go - Pan Fried Tu
 rnip Cakes with Preserved Sausage\n煎鮮蝦餅 Jyu Yuk Gau Choi Har Beng 
 - Pan Fried Pork & Chive Shrimp Patties\nTea: 鐵觀音 Tie Guan Yin - "Ir
 on Goddess" oolong tea\n銀針粉 XO Jeung Chau Ngan Jam Fun - Hand-Made S
 tir-Fried Silver Pin Noodles with XO Sauce\n鮮蝦腸 Har Cheung Fun - Shr
 imp Rice Rolls\n脆皮鮮蝦紅米腸 Chui Pei Hung Mai Har Cheung - Crisp
 y Shrimp Red Rice Roll\nTea: 壽眉 Sau Mei - a leafy white Tea\n黑金流
 沙包 Hak Gum Lau Sa Bao - Charcoal Molten Salted Egg Yolk Buns\n-----\nW
 ok TheoryOpened in 2023\, Wok Theory is owned by a second-generation husba
 nd-wife duo who seized an opportunity to redefine the culinary scene in To
 ronto's Chinatown. Balancing nostalgia and tradition with innovative moder
 n touches\, they are aiming to become a culinary destination for those sea
 rching for authentic Chinese cuisine and an elevated dim sum experience. w
 oktheory.com\n-----\nThe Depanneur is where Interesting Food Things happen
 . For more than a decade The Dep has been showcasing Toronto’s remarkabl
 e culinary diversity by hosting unique food events. @thedepanneur
LOCATION:Wok Theory
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-ultimate-dim-sum-experience-at-wok-t
 heory-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Walrus Talks AccessAbility
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T200000
UID:blogto-234244@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_image7b2aaa0b-4a11-4358-8f6e-d77e131123
 05.jpg
DESCRIPTION:According to the Canadian Survey on Disability\, 27% of Canadi
 ans over the age of fifteen identify as living with a disability—around 
 eight million people. In the age of the Accessible Canada Act\, the Canada
  Disability Benefit\, and Accessibility Standards Canada\, why is there a 
 gap between policy and people’s lived experience?\nThe Walrus Talks Acce
 ssAbility is a live podcast recording of Courage Inc. hosted by Duncan Sin
 clair\, Deloitte Chair of Canada and Chile\, who brings years of leadershi
 p and expertise to this urgent discussion. Featuring talks by four speaker
 s from the disability community on policy frameworks\, leadership\, and in
 novation\, the importance of technology\, corporate rollbacks on DEI\, and
  the persistence of ableism\, the talks will be followed by a panel discus
 sion moderated by Sinclair.\nAhead of National AccessAbility Week\, join u
 s for this special edition of The Walrus Talks in Toronto or online.
LOCATION:Bram and Bluma Appel Salon
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-walrus-talks-accessability-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trivia Tuesday May Social Mixer at Pizza Rustica
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T213000
UID:blogto-234623@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_imageb9e44492-0d4c-41d2-ba98-f0a7f7439d
 ce.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Tired of the same routines\, awkward meetups events\, or endle
 ssly scrolling for plans?\nWhether you’re new to Toronto\, looking to ex
