BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ficoa x Pompette Group: A French-Latin Culinary Exchange Launching
  a New Chef Collaboration Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T220000
UID:blogto-234792@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/07/original_imaged25c84ef-faa9-4056-8985-19d0c4ea65
 9e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A six-course tasting experience on May 27 brings together two 
 of Toronto’s leading culinary voices in a dialogue between ancestral ing
 redients and European influence\nToronto\, ON — May 7\, 2026 — Neo-Lat
 in fine dining destination Ficoa will host a one-night-only chef collabora
 tion with the renowned Pompette Group on Wednesday\, May 27\, bringing tog
 ether two of Toronto’s most dynamic culinary forces for an intimate\, si
 x-course tasting experience rooted in cultural exchange\, storytelling\, a
 nd technique. The Pompette Group\, whose Bar Pompette was recently named N
 o. 8 on North America’s 50 Best Bars 2026 list and No. 2 on Canada’s 1
 00 Best Bars\, joins Ficoa to kick off the restaurant’s new chef collabo
 ration series\, showcasing the group’s broader identity and savoir-faire
  across its portfolio\, which includes Bar Pompette\, Bakery Pompette\, an
 d the newly launched Bar Allegro.\nSet in Toronto’s Little Italy\, Ficoa
  has quickly established itself as a rising voice in the city’s dining s
 cene\, known for its refined yet soulful interpretation of Latin cuisine a
 nd its evolving\, ingredient-driven approach that balances tradition with 
 contemporary technique. Priced at $145 per person for the tasting menu (ex
 clusive of tax and gratuity)\, with optional beverage pairings available\,
  the evening will unfold across two seatings at 5:00 PM and 7:30 PM.\nAbou
 t the Collaboration\nThe evening will mark the first in a new series of ch
 ef collaborations at Ficoa\, an initiative designed to explore the diversi
 ty and evolution of Latin cuisine through dialogue with global culinary pe
 rspectives.\nEach collaboration invites a guest chef or group to engage wi
 th Ficoa’s approach\, creating one-night-only menus that reflect how Lat
 in American cuisine continues to evolve through technique\, migration\, an
 d cultural exchange.\nThe debut collaboration with Pompette Group is conce
 ived as a journey through the Americas\, expressed through the lens of Fre
 nch technique. The six-course menu traces a path across regions including 
 Mexico\, Peru\, and Argentina\, highlighting a dialogue between ancestral 
 ingredients and European culinary influence.\nStructured as an alternating
  exchange between chefs\, each course builds on the last\, revealing both 
 contrast and cohesion in a shared culinary language.\nMenu Overview\nThe s
 ix-course tasting menu is designed as a collaborative exchange between Fic
 oa and Pompette Group\, with alternating courses from each kitchen:\n\nL
 ’Amuse de la Milpa — Blue corn pâte brisée\, epazote-infused chèvre
 \, morita piloncillo gastrique\nCeviche de Altura — Seabass\, cucumber\,
  purple potato vichyssoise\, chulpi corn\, pickled sweet potato purée\nAs
 ado de Veau — Veal striploin\, gaucho-style sweetbreads\, malbec reducti
 on\, chimi-grenobloise\, celeriac purée\nShort Rib Bourguignon — Carame
 lised onion empanada\, mole jus\nHalibut — Guajillo lobster bisque\, pla
 ntain mousseline\, roasted fennel\, cilantro oil\, crispy salsa macha\nDar
 k Chocolate Ganache — Burnt pineapple\, grilled corn crème anglaise\, m
 asa tuile\, mezcal caramel\nTogether\, the menu reflects a seamless interp
 lay between French technique and Latin American ingredients\, moving from 
 land to sea to dessert in a progression that is both cohesive and explorat
 ory.\nEvent Details\nDate: Wednesday\, May 27\, 2026\nLocation: Ficoa\, 58
 5 College St\, Toronto\nSeatings: 5:00 PM & 7:30 PM\nFormat: Six-course ta
 sting menu\nPricing:\n$145 per person (tasting menu)\nOptional beverage pa
 iring: $50–$55\nTickets will be available via OpenTable.\nBeverage Progr
 am\nThe beverage program will be led by the Bar Pompette\, bringing its aw
 ard-winning approach to cocktails and wine into the experience. Pairings w
 ill include a mix of wine and cocktails\, with one pairing per course\, al
 ongside a non-alcoholic option.\nGuests will be welcomed with a cocktail f
 eaturing Valley of Mother of God Gin\, included in the ticket price.\nAbou
 t Chef Esau Garcia\nBorn in Camargo\, Chihuahua\, Chef Esau Garcia brings 
 over 13 years of international culinary experience spanning Mexico\, Austr
 alia\, and Canada. His work is defined by a balance of precision and emoti
 onal depth\, rooted in traditional Mexican cooking while shaped by global 
 technique.\nPrior to joining Ficoa\, Garcia held key roles in several of T
 oronto’s most recognized kitchens\, including Madrina Bar y Tapas\, Rosa
 linda\, and Lena. At Ficoa\, his approach reflects a commitment to honouri
 ng tradition while reinterpreting it through a contemporary lens.\nAbout C
 hef Martine Bauer\nChef Martine Bauer is Co-Founder of the Pompette Group\
 , the team behind award-winning Bar Pompette\, Bakery Pompette\, and Bar A
 llegro. Born in Mauritius and trained in Paris\, Bauer’s culinary perspe
 ctive is shaped by European technique and global experience.\nHer work is 
 grounded in precision\, seasonality\, and storytelling\, bringing together
  influences of migration and place through refined\, thoughtful execution.
 \nAbout Ficoa\nFicoa is a neo-Latin fine dining restaurant in Toronto’s 
 Little Italy\, founded by restaurateur Patricia Toro. Known for its evolvi
 ng\, ingredient-driven approach\, Ficoa explores Latin American cuisine th
 rough a contemporary lens\, balancing tradition with innovation in both it
 s tasting and à la carte offerings.\nAbout the Pompette Group\nThe Pompet
 te Group is a Toronto-based hospitality group behind Bar Pompette\, Bakery
  Pompette\, and Bar Allegro. Recognized internationally for its bar progra
 m and culinary perspective\, the group brings together European tradition 
 and modern hospitality.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ficoa-x-pompette-group-a-french-latin-cu
 linary-exchange-launching-a-new-chef-collaboration-series-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
