SUMMARY:Screen Life: A Free Digital Balance Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T110000
UID:blogto-234712@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/06/original_image9fd89f03-621f-4c45-81ee-e916265b2c
 7a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:You meant to check one thing on your phone. That was forty-fiv
 e minutes ago. You want better phone habits - you can't seem to get there.
 \nScreen Life is a free two-hour workshop with one rule: no shame\, no lec
 tures\, no detox dogma. Just practical\, honest strategies for living with
  the device in your pocket.\nPart of Toronto Tech Week 2026\, hosted by Of
 fline.now (https://Offline.now) and the University of Toronto's Schwartz R
 eisman Innovation Campus.\nYou'll hear from a curated lineup of practition
 ers on focus\, burnout\, relationships\, family\, and healthy AI use. You'
 ll take a quick personal assessment to see where you actually stand. Then 
 you'll walk out with a real plan that fits your real life - not someone el
 se's idea of what your screen time should look like.\nFor anyone who wants
  better phone habits. Capacity is limited\, so don't wait.
LOCATION:Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus\, University of Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/screen-life-a-free-digital-balance-works
 hop-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
