 b1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Whether you’re a Toronto trivia nerd or just here to guess t
 he memes\, there’s something for everyone — plus tea\, snacks and brag
 ging rights.\nWant to flex your knowledge of our city? Or just see how man
 y famous Torontonian hits you can guess? Then\, sign up for The Green Line
 ’s upcoming third spaces event.\nMark your calendars\, and join us every
  third or fourth Thursday of the month for low-key gatherings hosted by ou
 r community engagement producer Adele Lukusa.\nCome on down to Youngplace 
 at 180 Shaw St.\, Suite 314 (across from Trinity Bellwoods Park in West Qu
 een West) on Thursday\, May 28\, from 6 to 9 p.m. Then put on your best ga
 me face\, as we look to crown Toronto’s Next Top Municipal Menace — pr
 izes included! Compete by yourself or in a team with friends old and new. 
 We’ll be covering as much ground as we can\, from TTC history to iconic 
 memes\, so get to studying.\nSupplies\, tea and snacks are provided with y
 our ticket\, which costs $15 (there's a limited time offer of 2 for 1 tick
 ets so you can bring a friend for free) — so all that’s missing is you
 . Get tickets at THEGREENLINE.TO/events or here: https://www.eventbrite.ca
 /e/third-spaces-event-toronto-trivia-night-edition-tickets-1988527281629\n
