BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:King East Design District Neighbourhood Hop presented by DesignTO 
 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T210000
UID:blogto-234635@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_image35246df1-ae56-4400-8061-18d5df0a11
 3b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:It’s time to celebrate innovation\, design\, and community a
 t the annual King East Design District (KEDD) Neighbourhood Hop\, organize
 d by DesignTO\, in collaboration with Old Town Toronto BIA.\nThe KEDD Neig
 hbourhood Hop returns as an opportunity to explore the district\, and lear
 n about the products on show at 7 participating “Neighbourhood Hubs.” 
 Offerings span from furniture\, lighting\, and decor\, to kitchen applianc
 es and sustainable surfaces for architecture and design. Whether you hop b
 etween hubs or settle in at your favourite\, this special night brings tog
 ether designers\, design-lovers\, and curious creatives for an evening of 
 connection and discovery.\nBSH Experience & Design Centre\, 334 King Stree
 t East @ Parliament Street\nCandace & Basil\, 75 Ontario Street @ Richmond
  Street East\nCosentino City Toronto\, 143 Frederick Street @ Front Street
  East\nDesign Within Reach Toronto\, 214 King Street East @ Sherbourne Str
 eet\nEQ3\, 222 King Street East @ Sherbourne Street\nKPMB Architects\, 351
  King Street East @ Berkeley Street\nSub-Zero\, Wolf\, and Cove Showroom\,
  280 King Street East @ Ontario Street\nView Neighbourhood Hub Locations o
 n Google Maps\nThe KEDD Neighbourhood Hop is free\, but attendees need to 
 RSVP. Guests can check in at any Neighbourhood Hub to get a wristband\, an
 d then move between venues. Note each venue has unique capacity limits.\nM
 ore Details\nAt the BSH Experience & Design Centre Thermador showcases an 
 installation titled ‘Moonlight Blue’ curated by Kilowatt Kate. Enter a
  space of soft glowing illumination combining textiles\, fine crafted meta
 l\, rattan and bamboo with oceanic inspired accents where attendees feel t
 he influence of the pending full blue moon.\nCandace & Basil presents a de
 sign-forward experience\, highlighting luxury furniture crafted in Canada\
 , where quality\, comfort\, and customization converge.\nCosentino City To
 ronto presents the Maitake table by Patkau Architects\, a demonstration of
  its Ēclos surface material brought to life through design\, with remarks
  from John Patkau alongside Cosentino leadership.\n‘Sip and shop’ at D
 esign Within Reach Toronto to experience exceptionally crafted\, built-to-
 last\, and the best in authentic modern design.\nDuring a celebration of d
 esign with cocktails\, light bites and live music\, EQ3 offers a sneak pee
 k of new products\, with EQ3 President\, Head of R&D\, and others in atten
 dance.\nOpen house at KPMB Architects\, an award-winning studio that desig
 ns transformative spaces that shape cities\, communities and the built env
 ironment.\nSub-Zero\, Wolf\, and Cove Showroom offers an elevated\, hands-
 on experience where visitors can explore and learn about Sub-Zero\, Wolf\,
  and Cove appliances in a fully operational kitchen space.\n–––\nThe
  ‘King East Design District Neighbourhood Hop’\, presented by DesignTO
 \, is supported by the Old Town Toronto BIA.\nDesignTO is a charitable art
 s organization celebrating 16 years of designing a sustainable\, just\, an
 d joyful future. We curate exhibitions\, presentations and educational pro
 gramming to increase the public’s knowledge and appreciation of design. 
 As Canada’s largest annual design festival\, DesignTO has welcomed over 
 1.2 million attendees\, reached 2.6 billion people through media\, and sho
 wcased 7\,500+ artists and designers since 2011.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/king-east-design-district-neighbourhood-
 hop-presented-by-designto-2026-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
