DESCRIPTION:Cathedral Bluffs Symphony Orchestra Presents: Mahler’s “Re
 surrection” Symphony\nExperience one of the most powerful works in class
 ical music as the Cathedral Bluffs Symphony Orchestra closes its landmark 
 40th anniversary season with Symphony No. 2 (Resurrection) by Gustav Mahle
 r.\nFrom moments of deep introspection to a breathtaking\, triumphant fina
 le\, Mahler’s “Resurrection” Symphony is an emotional journey from d
 arkness to light—culminating in a powerful message of hope\, renewal\, a
 nd transcendence.\nThis monumental performance features soprano Emily Roch
 a and mezzo-soprano Queen Hezumuryango\, joined by the acclaimed Pax Chris
 ti Chorale\, under the direction of Artistic Director Elaine Choi.\nEvent 
 Details\nSaturday\, May 30\, 2026 – 8:00 PM\nP.C. Ho Theatre\, Chinese C
 ultural Centre of Greater Toronto\nWhy You Should Go\nA rare chance to hea
 r Mahler’s epic “Resurrection” Symphony performed live\nA massive or
 chestral and choral experience with over 100 performers on stage\nA deeply
  moving journey exploring life\, death\, and renewal\nThe grand finale of 
 CBSO’s 40th anniversary season\nTickets available now: cathedralbluffs.c
 om
LOCATION:Chinese Cultural Centre of Greater Toronto
