BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:L'Mina - Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T152500
UID:blogto-233870@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image57daab2f-15a0-4b5d-a2f5-c9cebac6b9
 5d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:25 minutes | Morocco\, Qatar\, Italy\, France | Arabic with En
 glish subtitles.\nA film by Randa Maroufi\, presented as part of Every Wor
 ker Should Have Equal\nLabour Rights\, curated by Nima Esmailpour.\nJerad 
 is a mining town in Morocco where coal extraction\, although officially ha
 lted in 2001\, continues informally to this day. L’Mina recreates the cu
 rrent work in informal mining pits using a set design created in collabora
 tion with the town’s residents\, who perform in their own roles.\nRegist
 er at mayworks.ca\nThis venue has wheelchair accessible bathrooms and a wh
 eelchair accessible venue.
LOCATION:Alliance Francaise Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/lmina-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
