ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/22/original_imagec2e4fa5c-9d10-45f8-aad1-9b11079b42
 1f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for Scottish Country Dancing which includes jig
 s\, reels\, and Ceilidh dances for all ages. We have a live band performin
 g with beginner and audience participation dances on the program.\nThis is
  a free event which is enjoyable to watch. It's great to come early and en
 joy Toronto's lovely Botanical Gardens.\nScottish Country Dancing is a won
 derful form of exercise as well as a great social activity. There are Scot
 tish Country Dance groups around the world and many are located in the Tor
 onto area.\nPlease come out for a fun evening. It's a treat to dance outsi
 de on the grass to live music.\nOur web site is dancescottish.ca
LOCATION:Edwards Gardens
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dancing-in-the-park-toronto-8/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Forest Raiser!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T210000
UID:blogto-234167@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/25/original_imagef2ef13cc-d4e2-40d3-919c-f1e07db293
 fe.jpg
DESCRIPTION:​Forest-Raiser. An evening to raise funds and awareness for 
 forest conservation and reforestation initiatives.\n​Forests are among o
 ur most vital ecosystems — providing habitat\, regulating climate\, and 
 sustaining life across the planet. This Toronto Climate Week\, we invite y
 ou to celebrate and support the organizations working to protect them.\n
 ​Mix and mingle over nature-inspired mocktails\, soulful jazz\, and plan
 t-forward delicacies. Immerse yourself in eco-arts and connect with like-m
 inded individuals.\n​Most important (!) Hear from three purpose-driven o
 rganizations and support their work through our silent auction.\n​This y
 ear’s beneficiaries are:\n​• FSC (Forest Stewardship Council) — Th
 e Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) sets the gold standard for responsible 
 forest management.\n​• Flash Forest — Modernizing forestry through d
 ata-driven automation.\n​• LEAF (Local Enhancement & Appreciation of F
 orests) — Engaging GTA communities in urban forest planting\, stewardshi
 p and education.\n​Forest-Raiser Tuesday\, June 2nd\, 2026 | 6:00 – 9:
 00 PM Centre for Social Innovation\, Toronto\n​We look forward to coming
  together for an evening that invests in our forests\, and the future they
  make possible for all species.\n​A huge thank you to our volunteers and
  sponsors making the event possible. Let’s toast one to the trees!
LOCATION:Centre for Social Innovation
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/forest-raiser-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
