BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hirut Ethiopian / Jazz Club presents NYC jazz pianist Ray Gallon\,
  Toronto bassist Mike Downes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T223000
UID:blogto-234357@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_imagea55d2e87-6e40-4ec7-a4c3-9d03e766c4
 e6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The evening showcases an intriguing blend of Ray's original co
 mpositions and fresh\, reimagined takes on classic standards.\nUK Jazz New
 s wrote: “ In Gallon’s playing there is amazing melodic clarity and in
 vention and intention. Pure joy. A very special gig.”\n“Extraordinary!
 ” Ahmad Jamal\nTo listen to pianist Ray Gallon is to take a journey thro
 ugh the great lineage of jazz piano from its inception all the way up to t
 he cutting-edge present. Imbued with the vocabulary\, sensibilities and so
 ul of the very architects of the jazz artform\, Gallon’s sound is right-
 at-home emanating from the strings of the piano at the iconic Van Gelder S
 tudios - emanating through the very room in which many of the classic jazz
  albums of yesteryear were recorded.\nGrand Company has garnered praise fr
 om GRAMMY winning pianist Bill Charlap for its exceptional trio concept. C
 harlap rhapsodizes in the liner notes of Ray’s recent release with Ron C
 arter and Lewis Nash: “This is my favorite kind of trio playing - the in
 imitable and distinctive personal and collective sound has transparency an
 d clarity\, where every note and gesture mean something. Ray Gallon’s mu
 sic is informed\, passionate\, and personal. He possesses a unique rhythmi
 c imagination and a wrought iron vocabulary.”\nHe will be joined by exce
 ptional jazz bassist Mike Downes\, well-known to Toronto jazz fans.
LOCATION:Hirut
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/hirut-ethiopian-jazz-club-presents-nyc-j
 azz-pianist-ray-gallon-toronto-bassist-mike-downes-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
