BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WORLD BELOVED: A CELEBRATION OF WOMEN COMPOSERS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T213000
UID:blogto-234727@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:In our final concert of the season\, ECC turns the spotlight o
 n contemporary women composers featuring local Canadian and internationall
 y recognized artists\, including ECC’s own Lauren Halász and Jade Lotte
 r.\nThis vibrant and diverse program centers on The World Beloved: A Blueg
 rass Mass by Carol Barnett\, with libretto by Marisha Chamberlain (2006). 
 This dynamic work blends the traditional form of the mass with the energy 
 and spirit of bluegrass\, featuring an instrumental ensemble of fiddle\, b
 anjo\, mandolin\, guitar\, and bass.\nThe program includes works by distin
 guished Canadian composers Eleanor Daley and Ruth Watson Henderson\, whose
  contributions have shaped the country’s choral landscape. We conclude t
 he evening with the spirited When I Become an Old Woman by Sherry Blevins
 —a joyful finale to a richly varied program.
LOCATION:Runnymede United Church
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/world-beloved-a-celebration-of-women-com
 posers-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You'll See
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T131500
UID:blogto-231955@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/09/original_image3fa3d857-6ff0-4c4c-8e84-9eea39291f
 76.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Ulysses for children? Yes\, Ulysses for children.\nJames Joyce
 ’s epic story of one day in one city is brought to life in this inventiv
 e new show\, bringing Ireland’s most notorious book to audiences aged 8 
 and upwards\, and to all those who haven’t got around to reading it yet.
 \nCombining live performance\, intricate paper design\, an original score 
 and Joyce’s odyssey\, this is theatre that will excite both young and ol
 d.\n“Ulysses for children: has the world gone mad?... Branar has gone an
