BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Caged Bird Sings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T210000
UID:blogto-234036@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/22/original_image0eabe880-90ec-4f13-8bf3-41087b2e61
 e2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Caged Bird Sings\nCreated by Rouvan Silogix\, Rafeh Mahmud
 \, and Ahad Lakhani\nDirected by Rafeh Mahmud\nTarragon Theatre Presents a
  Modern Times and Theatre ARTaud Production\nJune 9 – 21\, 2026\nWitness
  a radical re-imagining of Rumi’s “Masnavi”.\nThe Caged Bird Sings t
 ells the story of three prisoners: two star-crossed lovers and scientists 
 – Rumi and Jin – who share a cell with Sal\, a mysterious vagrant. As 
 they navigate their new-found reality and reconcile their past lives\, the
 y are haunted by ghosts and demons of their own making.\nThe Caged Bird Si
 ngs explores the literal and metaphorical prisons that we are put in\, put
  ourselves in\, and the ones that we create.  Inspired by Sufi mysticism a
 nd concepts of Fanafillah\, the critically-acclaimed production examines o
 ur ability to overcome and break out of the cage.
LOCATION:Tarragon Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-caged-bird-sings-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2nd World Summit on Smart Grid and Clean Energy Technologies
