ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/23/original_image44f66867-15ec-4c0c-87af-57b3f6223e
 79.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Discover the world premiere of Parḗlios\, a bold new Canadia
 n English language opera by composer Cecilia Livingston and librettist Dun
 can McFarlane. Blending opera\, installation\, and oratorio\, Parḗlios e
 xplores themes of migration\, climate change and humanity’s connection t
 o our planet earth through an immersive mix of music\, movement\, and visu
 al storytelling. With percussion\, choir\, and contemporary dance woven in
 to its fabric\, the work creates a vivid\, transformative experience that 
 pushes the boundaries of the operatic form.\nDirector & Choreographer: Jen
 nifer Nichols\nMusic Director: Evan Mitchell\nSet Designer: Carlyn Rahusaa
 r Routledge\nProjection Designer: Nathan Bruce\nLighting Designer: Siobhan
  Sleath\nCostume Designer: Chris Faris\nSoprano Soloist - Len Crino\nAlto 
 Soloist - Brenden Lengsfeld\nTenor Soloist - Ryan Nauta\nBaritone Soloist 
 - Aaron Dimoff\nDancers - Sully Malaeb Proulx\, Jarrett Siddall\, Miyeko F
 erguson\nFeaturing TorQ percussion ensemble\nPart of Opera 5’s 2026 Toro
 nto Opera Festival
LOCATION:Theatre Passe Muraille
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/parelios-by-cecilia-livingston-duncan-mc
 farlane-world-premiere-toronto/
