BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Art Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T160000
UID:blogto-234454@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_image529bdbe4-ff21-473a-80d1-d0a72f43c5
 8c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous Art Journey Returns to Toronto with Free Community 
 Event Celebrating Indigenous Artists\nToronto\, ON — Shawish Market is p
 roud to present the Indigenous Art Journey\, a free\, one-day community ev
 ent celebrating the beauty\, resilience\, and diversity of Indigenous arti
 stry for Indigenous History Month. Taking place on Sunday\, June 14\, 2026
 \, from 10:00 AM to 4:00 PM at the Toronto Reference Library\, the event w
 ill bring together over 20 Indigenous artists for a day of art\, culture\,
  and connection.\nDesigned to uplift Indigenous creators and provide acces
 sible cultural experiences for the public\, Indigenous Art Journey will fe
 ature a curated art exhibit\, a vendor marketplace\, and interactive works
 hops led by Indigenous artists. Admission is free\, with optional donation
 s supporting Shawish Market’s mission to maintain a zero-fee platform fo
 r Indigenous vendors.\n“Shawish Market was created to remove barriers fo
 r Indigenous artists\, and Indigenous Art Journey brings that vision into 
 a physical space where community can connect directly with creators and th
 eir stories\,” says Amanda Bernard\, Founder of Shawish Market. “We in
 tentionally designed this event to be free and accessible\, because experi
 encing Indigenous art and culture shouldn’t be limited by cost. Everyone
  is welcome to come\, learn\, and connect.”\nEvent Highlights:\n1. Curat
 ed Indigenous Art Exhibit showcasing works from emerging and established a
 rtists\n2. Vendor Marketplace featuring over 20 Indigenous-owned brands\n3
 . Beading Workshops led by renowned artists Joy Rogers and Saga Kwandibenz
 \n4. Free Coffee\, Tea & Pastries available to attendees throughout the da
 y\nThe Indigenous Art Journey reflects a growing movement toward ethical c
 onsumption and cultural appreciation\, offering attendees an opportunity t
 o engage directly with artists\, learn traditional practices\, and support
  authentic Indigenous businesses. Both Indigenous and non-Indigenous parti
 cipants are welcome.\nThis event builds on Shawish Market’s broader miss
 ion to empower Indigenous entrepreneurs across Turtle Island by eliminatin
 g vendor fees and fostering sustainable economic growth within communities
 .\nFor more information\, event details\, or to reserve a spot\, visit:  h
 ttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/indigenous-art-journey-presented-by-shawish-mar
 ket-tickets-1983491297866?aff=oddtdtcreator\nMedia Contact:\nAmanda Bernar
 d\nFounder\, Shawish Market\nshawish.market@gmail.com\nwww.shawishmarket.c
 om  / Instagram: @shawish.market
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/indigenous-art-journey-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
