ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/30/original_imagefaa14084-6bda-4d66-af11-d14a6438e4
 b7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Independent filmmaker Cameron Tingley presents LIFE AS WE KNOW
  IT\, a one-of-a-kind presentation using humorous short films that get peo
 ple talking about how mass culture shapes our relationships with each othe
 r\, with society at large\, and with the natural world. The films are prod
 uced with the theatrical troupe The Flying Spot Players. Topics include th
 e environment\, media awareness\, and social civility. FREE ADMISSION. www
 .facebook.com/pages/The-Flying-Spot-Players/1426632774242185
LOCATION:Forest Hill Public Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/life-as-we-know-it-screening-of-short-fi
 lms-toronto-6/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Myra Bloom: Evasive Manoeuvres: Canadian Women's Confessional Writ
 ing Author Talks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T200000
UID:blogto-233623@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image83b96528-782a-449c-b4e7-8e273e9a00
 e8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Confession is everywhere in our culture. It drives banal socia
 l media posts\, sensational reality television shows\, revolutionary socia
 l justice movements\, and popular fiction. It has also been central to fem
 inist movements throughout the twentieth and twenty-first centuries. But a
 cts of self-disclosure carry significant risks for women and nonbinary wri
 ters\, who may be disbelieved or retraumatized\, dismissed as narcissistic
  or unliterary\, or stereotyped in ways that constrain professional opport
 unities.\nNaming this tension the “confessional impasse\,” Myra Bloom 
 explores how four contemporary Canadian writers navigate both the possibil
 ities and the perils of confession. Focusing on the work of Tanya Tagaq\, 
 Nelly Arcan\, Sheila Heti\, and Sina Queyras\, Bloom offers a dynamic expl
 oration of confessional writing in poetry and autofiction\, a hybrid form 
 of life writing that blends autobiography with invention. She situates the
  forces increasingly shaping women’s lives – social media\, digital cu
 lture\, beauty culture\, and the relentless pressure to optimize the body 
 – within a broader ecosystem that demands self-display for public consum
 ption. Using the confessional impasse as a theoretical framework\, Bloom s
 hows that although writers deploy evasive manoeuvres to avoid rendering th
 emselves vulnerable\, they are often misread through the very autobiograph
 ical discourses they are escaping.\nAs Canadian literature becomes increas
 ingly confessional in its texts\, institutions\, and discourse\, Evasive M
 anoeuvres provides an exciting in-depth study of an overlooked force drivi
 ng literary innovation in Canada.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/myra-bloom-evasive-manoeuvres-canadian-w
 omens-confessional-writing-author-talks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Ballet of Canada: Maddaddam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T213000
UID:blogto-228659@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2025/12/31/original_imagea3f3c651-b66a-40c5-a8b6-3e65f3db38
 e9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:To experience MADDADDAM is to be immersed in the imagination a
 nd unflinching moral acuity of Canada’s Margaret Atwood on subjects of r
 ampant technological experimentation\, colonialism and greed. Wayne McGreg
 or’s 2022 co-production with The Royal Ballet brings Atwood’s post-apo
 calyptic MaddAddam trilogy to life\, exploring themes of extinction and in
 vention\, hubris and humanity\, spliced together with Atwood’s signature
  activism and connection to Canada. Scored by one of the greatest living c
 omposers\, Max Richter\, MADDADDAM is an unforgettable production for our 
 time.\nTickets available @ https://eventschaser.com/?s=Maddaddam+Toronto
LOCATION:Four Seasons Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/national-ballet-of-canada-maddaddam-toro
 nto-9/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Questionable - SAPPHIC OVER 30 EDITION : Queer Singles Trivia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T220000
UID:blogto-234834@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/08/original_imagefed4f7a5-0997-4654-939b-00b7d215dd
 38.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at GROUND CONTROL. This edition is for sapphics 30 yea
 rs or older. Always trans and enby inclusive.\nTired of the apps? Is Toron
 to a tough place to meet new people? Try this! QUESTIONABLE is trivia with
  a twist….\nAlready have what you're looking for but have a friend who y
 ou want to set up? Come pitch them!\nThis is our SAPPHIC EDITION. Always t
 rans and enby inclusive.\nCome be part of the series that has become the s
 tuff of legends.....\nTHIS IS OUR 30+ EDITION for GROWN sapphics who are 3
 0 and up!\nThis event is at\nGROUND CONTROL\n1279 Queen Street West\nDoors
  at 7:30pm\nFirst Round starts at 8pm\nHosted by your faves:\n@chaodykes\n
 How does it work?\nYou will be put in a team with 5-6 people you don’t k
 now.\nThere will be 2 rounds of trivia. Each round\, you will change teams
 !\nThere will be a DJ In the lounge after the event so you can stay after 
 the event to keep the conversations going!\nWhat does ‘single’ mean?\n
 'Single’ means you are open to connecting with other people for love\, l
 ust or friendship.\nMaybe you will meet your soulmate! Maybe you will meet
  your new best friend! Maybe you will make out in the bathroom! Maybe you 
 will add a lover to your rotation! Maybe you will find a gaming buddy. Que
 er love is EXPANSIVE. Let's be open to a variety of connections.\nThe even
 t is poly-friendly\, slut-friendly\, monogamy-friendly\, ace-friendly. If 
 you can’t leave your judgment of others at home\, then you should stay h
 ome.\nCost\nWe are doing a sliding scale of $7-$25.\nAnd you get a $2 cred
 it at the bar with this ticket purchase!\nAll funds are going to Glad Day 
 Lit to support 2SLGBTQ artists and community events.\nSchedule\n7:30pm - D
 oors Open\, you get put into your first team\n8pm - First Round starts\n10
 pm ISH - Expected end\, but you can stay to socialize!\nHow will you make 
 the teams?\nThe teams will mostly be random.\nHow many people can attend?\
 nOur max number for this event is 85 people.This event can sell out and th
 e lower price tickets sell out first\, so act fast.\nYou can email any que
 stions to have to: vip@gladday.ca
LOCATION:Ground Control
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/questionable-sapphic-over-30-edition-que
 er-singles-trivia-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:siofra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T210000
UID:blogto-233907@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_imagebe6ba9a5-793a-4190-a716-fb481ffa85
 4d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Following the critical acclaim of spindle collective’s first
  work\, SAMCA\, comes a new dark folklore play by Natalia Bushnik and Kath
 leen Welch. síofra follows a newlywed couple in Belclare\, Ireland\, in t
 he late 1800’s\, and the tragedy that occurs when they build a home on a
  supposed ‘fairy mound’ underneath the famed Knockma Hill. Exploring t
 he myth of Irish changelings\, síofra is Act II of the ‘Dark Mother Tri
 logy’\, a series of three horror-theatre plays exploring fertility and m
 otherhood through the dark folklore of three different countries: Romania 
 (SAMCA)\, Ireland (síofra)\, and Germany (spilleHOLLE). With an extremely
  talented ensemble cast and original music by Welch\, join us at the foot 
 of Knockma Hill\, Ireland for a play that is both sinister and mysterious.
LOCATION:The Red Sandcastle Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/siofra-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
