BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Adjuster
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T174500
UID:blogto-234625@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_imageacaeb3e9-5aa7-43fd-b474-f7d3f29220
 d4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Noah Render (Elias Koteas) is an insurance claims adjuster who
  attends to his clients’ every need—including their sexual ones. His w
 ife\, Hera (Arsinée Khanjian)\, is a government censor who spends her day
 s and nights obsessively watching pornography for both work and pleasure. 
 When they become involved with Bubba (Maury Chaykin) and Mimi (Gabrielle R
 ose)\, a wealthy couple with a taste for kinky role-playing\, the Renders
 ’ lives are turned upside down in this surreal puzzle from Atom Egoyan. 
 Criterion Collection\nPhoto Courtesy of Johnnie Eisen\, © Ego Film Arts
LOCATION:Hot Docs Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-adjuster-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TIME AND TRANSFORMATION
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T220000
UID:blogto-231314@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/23/original_imageb54a9207-96fa-467a-b2ed-b372d7c7fe
 a9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Hungarian composer Erno Dohnanyi’s Symphonic Minutes is divi
 ded into five movements\, each only one or two minutes in length. Each mov
 ement retains a typically classical form\, including a rhapsody\, a scherz
 o\, a theme and variations\, as well as a rondo. Michael Berkovsky and Cor
 al Solomon then perform Poulenc’s Concerto for two pianos and orchestra.
  Inspired by Mozart and Balinese gamelan\, the work features lively rhythm
 s\, graceful melodies\, and playful dialogue between the two pianos and or
 chestra\, blending wit\, lyricism\, and brilliance. Finnish composer Jean 
 Sibelius structured his Symphony no. 2 from a rising three-note motif out 
 of which all other themes are generated—a compositional practice Arnold 
 Schoenberg described as “developing variation.” The first movement als
 o bears a relationship to Richard Strauss’ famous tone poem\, Tod und Ve
 rklärung: both have the main theme emerge in full only at the end\, rathe
 r than the beginning.\nKristian Alexander | conductor\nMichael Berkovsky 
 – Coral Solomon | piano duo\nDaniel Vnukowski | host\n7:10 p.m. Prélude
 : pre-concert recital.\n7:20 p.m. Pre-concert talk.\nIntermission discussi
 on and Q&A with Michael Berkovsky\, Coral Solomon and Daniel Vnukowski.
LOCATION:Meridian Arts Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/time-and-transformation-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: Seminar: All About Alocasias Plants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T160000
UID:blogto-234541@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/03/original_imagee0811610-4c61-4d08-9bbd-61075cf35c
 ac.jpg
DESCRIPTION:All About Alocasias: How to Grow (and Keep Alive) These Tropic
 al Showstoppers\nStruggling with Alocasias? You’re not alone. These bold
 \, beautiful tropicals are known for their dramatic leaves and their equal
 ly dramatic care needs. All About Alocasias is an informative\, beginner-f
 riendly seminar designed to help you understand what these plants actually
  want so you can stop guessing and start growing with confidence.\nWe’ll
  break down the key factors that make or break an Alocasia\, from watering
  and light to humidity and dormancy. Whether your plant is dropping leaves
 \, turning yellow\, or just not thriving\, this session will help you get 
 to the root of the issue and bring it back on track.\nFor more details & t
 o sign up\, visit our website! www.angasfarm.ca
