ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image403a06ac-28f0-4805-a79c-9a265b847e
 46.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Noah Render (Elias Koteas) is an insurance claims adjuster who
  attends to his clients’ every need—including their sexual ones. His w
 ife\, Hera (Arsinée Khanjian)\, is a government censor who spends her day
 s and nights obsessively watching pornography for both work and pleasure. 
 When they become involved with Bubba (Maury Chaykin) and Mimi (Gabrielle R
 ose)\, a wealthy couple with a taste for kinky role-playing\, the Renders
 ’ lives are turned upside down in this surreal puzzle from Atom Egoyan. 
 Criterion Collection\nPair with Curious Minds // Toronto: Cinema City - wi
 th Eric Veillette - Week 3: Classified by the Ontario Board of Censors (Sa
 turday\, June 20).
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-adjuster-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Summer and Shade Community Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T190000
UID:blogto-231832@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/06/original_image89d3863f-bb6e-4c97-a8e0-63256bb341
 c8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This massive community market is taking over Etobicoke this Ju
 ne\nIf you're looking for the ultimate way to kick off your summer without
  spending a dime on admission\, a vibrant new community market is headed t
 o Etobicoke.\nPresented by Moonshadow Events\, the Summer & Shade Communit
 y Market is set to transform the Dundas West and Mabelle Avenue area into 
 a bustling hub of creativity and local talent. Whether you're a hardcore a
 rt collector or just looking for a unique weekend plan\, this all-ages eve
 nt is packing a lot into a single afternoon.\nShop Local\, Get Creative\nT
 he market will feature over 30+ local vendors and artists from across Etob
 icoke\, showcasing everything from unique exotic crafts to handmade jewelr
 y. But it’s not just about browsing\; it’s about doing.\nThe event is 
 hosting a series of hands-on ART Workshops where you can:\nFinally learn t
 o paint a canvas like a pro.\nCraft your very own emotional support pickle
  (the DIY companion we all clearly need).\nDesign and create custom pieces
  in a jewelry-making session.\nFood\, Art\, and Vibes\nBeyond the shopping
 \, expect immersive art installations and plenty of food and drinks to kee
 p you fueled while you explore. If you're looking for some spiritual insig
 ht\, professional tarot readers will be on-site offering readings in both 
 Spanish and English. It’s a rare chance to support neighborhood talent w
 hile picking up a new skill—or a glimpse into your future—all in one s
 pot.\nSummer & Shade Community Market\nWhen: June 27th\, 2026\nTime: 12 p.
 m. to 7 p.m.\nWhere: 5005 Dundas Street West & 47 Mabelle Ave\, Etobicoke\
 nPrice: Free entry!
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-summer-and-shade-community-market-to
 ronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: A Hands-On Bonsai Workshop for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T170000
UID:blogto-234542@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/03/original_imageb8e0f732-cd9e-446b-b408-ba65a6e9da
 35.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Bonsai Styling Workshop: Create\, Pot\, Wire & Trim Your Own B
 onsai!\nHave you ever wanted to try repotting or wiring a Bonsai but didn
 ’t know where to start? Or maybe you're excited to create your very own 
 Bonsai tree from scratch? This hands-on workshop is perfect for beginners 
 and anyone eager to dive into the art of Bonsai care and styling!\nIn this
  interactive\, hands-on workshop\, you'll create your very own Bonsai from
  start to finish. You’ll begin with a young Bonsai plant and\, under the
  guidance of an experienced Bonsai practitioner\, you will:\nChoose your p
 lant: Select from two different Bonsai plant varieties (Juniper\, Ficus or
  Jade).\nPot your plant: Transplant your selected Bonsai into a beautiful 
 5" ceramic pot with a saucer\, using the proper Bonsai soil.\nWire your Bo
 nsai: Learn the technique of wiring your Bonsai to train it into the shape
  and style you desire\, helping it take on its signature sculptural form.\
 nTrim and shape: Gain hands-on experience trimming and shaping your Bonsai
  to promote health and achieve a balanced aesthetic.\nYou will leave the w
 orkshop with your very own styled Bonsai tree in a decorative ceramic pot\
 , equipped with all the skills to continue nurturing and styling it at hom
 e.\nThe workshop is designed to give you practical\, hands-on experience\,
  working with the tools and techniques required to care for and shape your
  Bonsai from scratch. All materials and tools are provided\, including a 5
 " ceramic pot with saucer\, Bonsai soil\, wiring tools\, and your plant.\n
 For more details & to sign up\, visit our website! www.angasfarm.ca
LOCATION:Anga's Farm & Nursery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/angas-farm-a-hands-on-bonsai-workshop-fo
 r-beginners-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
